      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are correct to point out the nuance; many modern originalists adopt a textualist approach that treats the prefatory \"well-regulated militia\" clause as descriptive rather than limiting the operative \"right of the people.\" They argue that the text supports an individual right to keep and bear arms rooted in historical patterns of self-defense, not solely militia service. Living constitutionalists, while not always purely pragmatic, often ground their arguments in implied republican ideals or a broader commitment to dynamic constitutionalism, where the document is seen as a living framework for ordered liberty. The standoff thus becomes: is the document a fixed historical contract or an evolving standard for human rights within American governance?",
